          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often do they recheck it?",
          "answer": "The guidance I found says the thyroid-stimulating hormone test is usually repeated six to eight weeks after starting thyroid hormone medicine or after any change in its dose. This comes from the \"Hypothyroidism: which test comes first, and the monitoring interval after a change\" guidance (Endocrinology and thyroid association, educational summary). It also says an abnormal result is usually confirmed with a repeat test after several weeks before long-term treatment starts, because thyroid levels can shift during illness and through the day.\n\nThe retrieved text does not say how often the test is repeated once your levels are stable. Your clinician can tell you that schedule and whether your situation needs anything different.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
