          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Does it ever go back to normal?",
          "answer": "The search did not find an answer to this. The reference \"Hypothyroidism (underactive thyroid)\" cuts off before it covers outlook, so I can't tell you from these sources whether thyroid levels return to normal.\n\nThe passage I did get says primary hypothyroidism, where the thyroid gland itself is the problem, accounts for the great majority of cases. It also says central hypothyroidism, where the pituitary or hypothalamus is the problem, is uncommon.\n\nAsk your clinician:\n- What type of underactive thyroid do I have, and what does that mean for the outlook?\n- Is treatment expected to be long-term, and what would make that change?\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
